# tools/al/ales_reverb_time_witness.rish -- the reverb in real time: a Schroeder network named in milliseconds (resonance-audio).
#
# Chapter: the Six-Chapter double-seat, Chapter C thread (Resonance - the creative suite) - waymark resonance-audio - rung resonance-audio.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-094453_fill-ales188-resonance-reverb-in-real-time.md
# Stands on: resonance/reverb.rye (resonance-audio -- the Schroeder network this speaks in real time, delegated unchanged); resonance/clock.rye (resonance-audio --
# the sample clock, its samples_for converting ms to a bounded sample count); resonance/multitap_time.rye (resonance-audio -- the bank-converting twin
# this mirrors exactly).
#
# resonance/reverb_time.rye gives the resonance-audio reverb a face in milliseconds, mirroring multitap_ms over the multi-tap. reverb_ms converts
# start_ms, count_ms, and every comb's and allpass's delay_ms through resonance-audio's proven clock.samples_for into an index-named comb bank and
# allpass bank and delegates to resonance-audio's reverb UNCHANGED, so the millisecond-named reverb lands BYTE-FOR-BYTE the same samples as the
# index-named reverb over the converted delays and span. The selftest proves: the clock adds only units (both tools run, resonance-audio's exact
# hand value [-8000,0,10000,-1333,8000,2000,5056,1000]); at 48 kHz 1 ms converts to 48 samples and the first recirculation sits exactly
# there; a sub-sample comb (0 ms) refuses BadDelay rather than silently doing nothing; a stage delay past the clip refuses
# DurationTooLong; an empty comb bank refuses NoCombs, an over-long bank TooManyStages, a feedback at unity BadGain, an out-of-range span
# BadRange. Purely local -- the clock a samples-per-second count, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_reverb_time_witness.rish

say "ales-reverb-time: Language EN — resonance-audio seated the reverb (Schroeder's network — parallel combs summed then diffused through series allpasses) and resonance-audio carried it into stereo, but every comb and allpass delay is a count of sample INDICES. A keeper names a room in TIME — the pre-delays and decays of a hall are milliseconds, not sample counts — and the one missing fact is the sample rate, which resonance-audio's validated Clock holds. reverb.rye's own header named this rung; every index-named rung has earned its real-time twin this way: echo_ms over the echo, multitap_ms over the multi-tap, and now reverb_ms over the whole network."
say "ales-reverb-time: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: the CLOCK ADDS ONLY THE UNITS, NEVER THE AUDIO. reverb_ms converts start_ms, count_ms, and every stage's delay_ms through resonance-audio's samples_for into an index-named comb bank and allpass bank and delegates to resonance-audio's reverb unchanged, so the millisecond-named reverb lands byte-for-byte the same samples as the index-named reverb over the converted delays and span; a sub-sample stage converts to zero and refuses BadDelay honestly, rather than silently doing nothing."
say "ales-reverb-time: Lens TAME — one clip of i16 PCM, a validated clock, two bounded stack banks of at most reverb.max_stages timed stages each a u32 delay_ms and a plain u32/u32 fraction; the bank counts are checked before any conversion, each delay converted into a bounded stack bank, then the proven reverb run; DurationTooLong from the clock and NoCombs / TooManyStages / BadDelay / BadGain / BadRange from the reverb forward by name before any write, the clip untouched on refusal; siloed to resonance/, no new arithmetic on the audio path, no network, no keys, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
# THE BINARY LANDS IN A PEN, NEVER A SHARED PATH IN THE TREE (REDS %700). A fixed path is
# one name every run in this checkout writes: one run EXECUTES it while another's linker
# opens it, and the linker refuses with ETXTBSY -- so the guard answers differently on
# bytes nobody changed. `printf %s` trims the newline a bare capture would keep.
let pen = run ["sh" "-c" "printf %s $(mktemp -d)"]
assert pen.ok else "could not make a build pen: ${pen.err_brief}"
let bin = "${pen.out}/reverb_time"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p resonance/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} sh tools/fixtures/r/rye_build.sh resonance/reverb_time.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-reverb-time: build failed — ${build.err_brief}"

let outfile = "resonance/bin/reverb_time.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-reverb-time: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-reverb-time: ${shown.out_brief}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-reverb-time' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-reverb-time: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-reverb-time line"

# This rung delegates to resonance-audio's reverb over its public API -- re-prove the index-named reverb still stands green beside it.
let reverb = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} sh tools/fixtures/r/rye_build.sh resonance/reverb.rye -femit-bin=resonance/bin/reverb && resonance/bin/reverb selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN ales-reverb' && echo yes"]
assert (trim reverb.out) == "yes" else "ales-reverb-time: the resonance-audio reverb regressed under its real-time twin"

say "ales-reverb-time: GREEN — the reverb in real time: a Schroeder network named in milliseconds, a thin twin over resonance-audio exactly as multitap_ms is over the multi-tap. The clock adds only the units, never the audio: reverb_ms converts start_ms, count_ms, and every comb's and allpass's delay_ms through resonance-audio's samples_for and delegates to resonance-audio's reverb unchanged, so the millisecond-named reverb lands byte-for-byte the same samples as the index-named reverb (resonance-audio's exact hand value [-8000,0,10000,-1333,8000,2000,5056,1000]); at 48 kHz 1 ms converts to 48 samples and the first recirculation sits exactly there; a sub-sample comb refuses BadDelay, a stage delay past the clip DurationTooLong, an empty comb bank NoCombs, an over-long bank TooManyStages, a feedback at unity BadGain, an out-of-range span BadRange, each leaving the clip untouched; the resonance-audio reverb stays GREEN beside it. The stereo twin stereo_reverb_ms (the shared bank converted once, then resonance-audio's stereo_reverb) is the next thin rung, a named-room preset the higher-Lindy move after it."

# The pen is swept here rather than left for the next run to meet.
let pen_swept = run ["sh" "-c" "rm -rf ${pen.out}"]
assert pen_swept.ok else "the build pen outlived its witness: ${pen_swept.err_brief}"
